## Anti-patterns

- Agent as authorization authority.
- Prompt as RBAC.
- Shared agent account used to bypass per-user permissions.
- Memory as operational source of truth.
- Uploading DB dumps instead of using authoritative APIs.
- Adding tools without owner/source/allowlist/AuthZ.
- Enabling Slack by silently switching identity model.
- Enabling schedules/API triggers without actor semantics.
- Treating Preview as publication/go-live.
- Treating agent persona/icon as security metadata.
- Inventing provider UI steps not observed/currently supported.
- Expanding to writes without PREPARE/ACT/idempotency/postcondition governance.
